For code points in this range, `get_idna_map` uses `idna_map_8`. The `_fill_map` function handles this case:

```c
if (c <= 0xFF)
{
    map->cp1 = p[0];
    map->range = p[1];
    p += 2;
}
```

This reads 2 bytes for the header. Then:

```c
value = p[0];
```

This reads 1 byte for the value. So each entry in `idna_map_8` is 5 bytes.

The `_compare_idna_map` function for this case:

```c
