`map_is` is defined as:

```c
static inline int map_is (IDNAMap * m, unsigned flags)
{
    return (idna_flags[m->flag_index] & flags) == flags;
}
```

This checks if all the specified flags are set in `idna_flags[m->flag_index]`. The result depends on `m->flag_index` and `idna_flags`.

If `get_idna_map` returns the same `flag_index` for the same code point in both loops, then `map_is` should return the same result. And `get_idna_map` is deterministic, so this should be the case.

